# "Whenever this artifact or another artifact you control enters": Bot2's Mox Emerald entering does not trigger it and neither does Bot1's own Mountain (a land, not an artifact) - the stack is empty each time.
# Bot1's Haywire Mite, an artifact creature, does: the target must be a creature Bot1 controls (Bot2's Elvish Mystic is refused, the Mite itself chosen), so the freshly cast Mite gets +1/+0 and haste and
# attacks for 2 on the turn it came in. It is the fourth artifact (with the two Moxen and the Device), so the Device also transforms into Geode Grotto.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Dowsing Device
Haywire Mite
Mountain
Mountain x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Elvish Mystic
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dowsing Device.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Dowsing Device.Types = Artifact
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 0
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
? Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Haywire Mite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic)
Bot1.Target(Haywire Mite)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Attack(Haywire Mite > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 18
Bot1.Battlefield.Geode Grotto.Types = Land
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 5
